 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:14:56.549270Z",
 "text": "This clause is enforceable because it mirrors the statutory entry rights granted to landlords under the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*. Under subsection 26(3), once a landlord and tenant have agreed to terminate a tenancy (or a notice of termination has been given), the landlord is permitted to enter the rental unit without written notice between 8:00 a.m. and 8:00 p.m. to show it to prospective tenants, provided the landlord informs or makes reasonable efforts to inform the tenant before entering.\n\nVerdict: enforceable\nSection: 26",
